.TH RNDIS-TETHER 1 "2026-11-06" "TetherMac" "General Commands Manual"
.SH NAME
rndis-tether \- USB tethering from Android phones on macOS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rndis-tether
[\fB\-rwa4v\fR]
[\fB\-U\fR \fIuser\fR]
[\fB\-W\fR \fIuser\fR]
[\fB\-d\fR \fIvid\fR:\fIpid\fR]
.br
.B rndis-tether
\fB\-\-version\fR | \fB\-V\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rndis-tether
gives the Mac internet access through an Android phone's USB tethering, without any kernel extension.
It speaks RNDIS to the phone through libusb, handles DHCP, ARP and IPv6 neighbor discovery itself,
and exposes the link as a
.BR utun (4)
interface.
.PP
It must run as root.
It is normally installed as a LaunchDaemon by
.B tethermac-install
(or
.BR install.sh ),
with the options
.BR "\-r \-w \-a" .
.PP
The program is split in two processes.
A small
.I supervisor
runs as root: it creates the interface, applies network configuration after validating every value,
and cleans up.
A
.I worker
runs as an unprivileged user and does all the parsing of data coming from the phone and the network.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-r
Send all traffic through the phone (split routes 0.0.0.0/1 and 128.0.0.0/1, and ::/1 and 8000::/1 for IPv6)
and apply the phone's DNS server.
Both are removed when the session ends.
.TP
.B \-w
Wait for a phone and reconnect after it is unplugged.
.TP
.B \-a
Enable USB tethering on the phone with
.BR adb (1)
when no RNDIS device is found. USB debugging must be enabled and authorised.
.TP
.B \-4
IPv4 only: do not relay IPv6.
.TP
.B \-O
Accept a phone subnet that overlaps a network already connected to the Mac.
By default such a subnet is refused, so that a malicious phone cannot shadow a local network.
.TP
.BI \-U " user"
User that runs
.BR adb .
Defaults to
.IR SUDO_USER ;
required when started by launchd.
.TP
.BI \-W " user"
Unprivileged user of the worker process. Defaults to
.IR nobody .
.TP
.BI \-d " vid:pid"
Only use the device with this USB identifier (hexadecimal), for example
.IR 04e8:6864 .
.TP
.B \-v
Verbose logs.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/log/rndis-tether.log
Log of the service. Lines are tagged [root] or [worker].
.TP
.I /Users/Shared/rndis-tether.disabled
If this file exists, the service stays idle. The menu bar app creates and removes it.
.TP
.I /Users/Shared/rndis-tether.status
Current state, written by the supervisor every few seconds.
.TP
.I /Library/LaunchDaemons/io.github.rndis-tether.plist
launchd job of the service.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal end.
.TP
.B 1
No RNDIS device found (without \fB\-w\fR), session failure, or startup failure.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.TP
.B 70
The worker could not drop its privileges.
.SH SECURITY
Only the supervisor has root privileges. It accepts five kinds of requests from the worker and validates
the values of each of them before running
.BR ifconfig (8),
.BR route (8),
.BR scutil (8)
or
.BR adb (1).
See
.I SECURITY.md
and
.I docs/how-it-works.md
in the source distribution.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR adb (1),
.BR ifconfig (8),
.BR route (8),
.BR scutil (8)
.PP
